{
  "summary": "Makes LevelDB point-read and deserialization failures fatal directly inside CDBWrapper, notifying the owner's kernel notifications interface and aborting. Extends fatal failure handling to txindex consistency and block-file read errors during transaction lookups. Eliminates CCoinsViewErrorCatcher by connecting the coins cache directly to CCoinsViewDB, removes HaveCoin from the backing coin view, and marks coin view lookups noexcept.",
  "problem": "Previously, CDBWrapper::Read() returned false on deserialization failures (masking corruption as missing keys) and threw LevelDB point-read exceptions that callers could catch, allowing corrupted index lookups to fail individual RPC requests while the node continued running with damaged storage. Additionally, chainstate required a dedicated CCoinsViewErrorCatcher view layer solely to intercept read errors.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'A corrupt txindex point read can consequently fail one RPC while the node continues running. #35728 reports other txindex lookup failures as errors that callers can also catch while the node continues running.'",
    "Commit 45ab8a7012: 'When a txindex point read encounters a corrupt LevelDB table, the RPC reports the error and the node continues running. CDBWrapper::Read() throws on a LevelDB failure without notifying the database owner and reports a corrupt value as a missing key.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Touches database wrappers across chainstate, block storage, and all secondary index subsystems (txindex, coinstatsindex, blockfilterindex, txospenderindex). Startup point-read failures will now abort rather than reaching the GUI's database rebuild prompt.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Expanded scope to make txindex transaction lookup failures (including block-file read errors and consistency mismatches) fatal through BaseIndex fatal error reporting before aborting.",
  "card": "Makes LevelDB point-read and deserialization failures fatal inside CDBWrapper by logging the path and error, firing kernel fatal error notifications, and aborting. It also makes txindex consistency and block-file read failures fatal, eliminates the CCoinsViewErrorCatcher view layer, restricts HaveCoin to CCoinsViewCache, and marks coin view lookups noexcept. Previously, corrupt index reads or block-file read errors could fail single RPC queries while leaving a damaged node running, or mask corrupt UTXO entries as absent keys.",
  "needs": [],
  "confidence": "high",
  "uncertainties": [],
  "risk": {
    "level": "medium",
    "touches": ["validation", "rpc_api", "gui"],
    "why": "A false-positive fatal error or unexpected exception escaping a noexcept coin-view lookup will immediately crash the node."
  }
}
